@startuml
title Data-Flow Diagram — Level 2 (Translation and Validation Detail)

skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam rectangleBorderThickness 1
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Input question" as Input
rectangle "2.1 Identify target\nclass and terms" as P21
rectangle "2.2 Retrieve exact\nschema fingerprint" as P22
rectangle "2.3 Add few-shot\nexamples and rules" as P23
rectangle "2.4 Ask LLM for\nOksQuery / IR" as P24
rectangle "2.5 Normalize and\nvalidate AST against schema" as P25
rectangle "Decision: valid?" as Decision
rectangle "2.6 Build repair prompt\nwith diagnostic" as P26
rectangle "2.7 Compile validated\nOksQuery" as P27
rectangle "Approved query\nto executor" as Output
database "D1: Version-scoped\nschema index" as Schema
rectangle "LLM API" as LLM

Input --> P21
P21 --> P22
P22 --> Schema : lookup by terms
Schema --> P22 : classes, attributes, relations
P22 --> P23
P23 --> P24 : bounded prompt
P24 --> LLM : question + schema slice
LLM --> P24 : candidate output
P24 --> P25
P25 --> Decision
Decision --> P27 : yes
Decision --> P26 : no / diagnostic
P26 --> P24 : retry, max configured attempts
P27 --> Output

note right of P25
  Deterministic checks enforce class names,
  attribute names, operators, scope, and
  logical-expression structure.
end note

note left of Output
  No execution occurs until
  this validation boundary passes.
end note
@enduml
